  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Child labour free childcare</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The childcare sector procures different products from the 13 high risk sectors listed in the Government Gazette, including garment, toys, wooden furniture and tropical fruit. The sector is a large buyer of these products. As an end user, they are at the end of the value chain. Also, their clients are the consumers of tomorrow.As a sector, the sector has a lot of purchasing power, they want to create leverage, to improve labour and environmental conditions in those value chains by working and coordinating as a sector. The purpose is to use this purchasing power to have direct impact in the working conditions of especially smallholder farmers and their families.</narrative>
  </description>
